00:59:05,936 --> 00:59:07,206
(Rechecking the route)

1731
00:59:07,336 --> 00:59:08,376
What? Hold on.

1732
00:59:08,646 --> 00:59:09,706
The second one is...

1733
00:59:09,906 --> 00:59:11,146
Yes. Hello.

1734
00:59:11,846 --> 00:59:14,316
- He's just marching off. He is.
- Yes.

1735
00:59:14,876 --> 00:59:16,945
Do you know how to get there, Jae Seok?

1736
00:59:16,946 --> 00:59:18,816
Yeon Shik said it was this way, didn't you?

1737
00:59:19,356 --> 00:59:20,656
Yeon Shik, are we on the right track?

1738
00:59:22,886 --> 00:59:24,355
It's better to go through that alleyway.

1739
00:59:24,356 --> 00:59:26,695
- Come on, Yeon Shik.
- We were in the right direction.

1740
00:59:26,696 --> 00:59:28,026
(Making a U-turn, following Navi Yoo's lead)

1741
00:59:30,326 --> 00:59:32,836
- Do we have to cross the road?
- Yes. Then we go that way.

1742
00:59:33,036 --> 00:59:34,435
- Which way?
- We cross and go back?

1743
00:59:34,436 --> 00:59:35,466
Yes.

1744
00:59:35,866 --> 00:59:37,506
We could've just kept going straight.

1745
00:59:39,006 --> 00:59:41,205
- Like I said, we could do that too.
- I see.

1746
00:59:41,206 --> 00:59:43,675
- But it's a small detour.
- Is this closer?

1747
00:59:43,676 --> 00:59:44,676
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1748
00:59:44,677 --> 00:59:46,116
- Then this is the right way.
- Yes.

1749
00:59:47,076 --> 00:59:49,085
You're so handsome. Goodness.

1750
00:59:49,086 --> 00:59:50,686
- Hello.
- Excuse me.

1751
00:59:50,786 --> 00:59:53,216
- Why did you respond to her?
- Gosh. Thanks.

1752
00:59:53,356 --> 00:59:54,656
- Thank you.
- Come on, Yeon Seok.

1753
00:59:55,226 --> 00:59:56,726
- Why?
- Come on.

1754
00:59:57,026 --> 00:59:58,696
Why do you think she was talking to you?

1755
00:59:59,556 --> 01:00:01,225
- Come on, Yeon Seok.
- Well...

1756
01:00:01,226 --> 01:00:02,726
Our eyes met.

1757
01:00:02,996 --> 01:00:04,565
- You didn't have eye contact.
- I mean...

1758
01:00:04,566 --> 01:00:06,166
- Our eyes didn't meet.
- Exactly.

1759
01:00:06,536 --> 01:00:08,805
- Anyway, - I thanked her right away.

1760
01:00:08,806 --> 01:00:11,236
Yeon Seok won the situation.

1761
01:00:12,006 --> 01:00:13,076
I'll give him that.

1762
01:00:15,946 --> 01:00:18,476
Now, before we leave today,

1763
01:00:18,746 --> 01:00:21,376
let's clear Round Three at this spot.

1764
01:00:22,186 --> 01:00:23,546
It's from Kwon Soon Ah.

1765
01:00:24,146 --> 01:00:27,416
"Their black eyes are fixed on their moms 24 hours."

1766
01:00:27,686 --> 01:00:30,686
"Their big ears perk up at the faintest footsteps."

1767
01:00:31,126 --> 01:00:34,096
"They come running toward us whenever and wherever they are."

1768
01:00:34,426 --> 01:00:36,896
"These big and cute fluffballs..."

1769
01:00:37,126 --> 01:00:38,635
"bring us happiness just by existing."

1770
01:00:38,636 --> 01:00:40,196
- Puppies?
- I think they're puppies.

1771
01:00:40,436 --> 01:00:44,066
"Come and get your dose of cuteness therapy."

1772
01:00:44,406 --> 01:00:45,406
- Are they dogs?
- Dogs?

1773
01:00:45,407 --> 01:00:47,136
I think we'll meet some puppies.

1774
01:00:47,936 --> 01:00:49,605
- Don't tell me they're hairy...
- No?

1775
01:00:49,606 --> 01:00:51,106
- old men.
- Fluffballs?

1776
01:00:51,346 --> 01:00:52,846
- Hairy old men.
- Cats?

1777
01:00:53,776 --> 01:00:56,285
We thought they'd be puppies.

1778
01:00:56,286 --> 01:00:58,346
(What are these big and adorable fluffballs?)

1779
01:00:58,616 --> 01:00:59,985
- Hello.
- Hi.

1780
01:00:59,986 --> 01:01:01,955
This path must be fantastic...

1781
01:01:01,956 --> 01:01:03,685
- in spring.
- Gosh. It's pretty.

1782
01:01:03,686 --> 01:01:05,495
- This is nice.
- It's well-decorated.

1783
01:01:05,496 --> 01:01:07,356
It's perfect for walking and running.

1784
01:01:07,856 --> 01:01:09,225
Gosh. It's perfect in the fall.

1785
01:01:09,226 --> 01:01:11,066
Goodness. Listen to the steam.

1786
01:01:11,426 --> 01:01:12,836
Gosh. It's so pretty here.

1787
01:01:14,536 --> 01:01:18,036
Goodness. That puppy is taking such a calm stroll.

1788
01:01:18,306 --> 01:01:19,536
- Yeon Shik.
- Yes?

1789
01:01:19,676 --> 01:01:21,306
We're not taking a walk right now.

1790
01:01:21,706 --> 01:01:22,975
That puppy was so...

1791
01:01:22,976 --> 01:01:24,705
- Will you hurry, Yeon Shik?
- It was so calm.

1792
01:01:24,706 --> 01:01:27,016
- He was walking so calmly.
- If it was this far,

1793
01:01:27,246 --> 01:01:29,216
we should've grabbed a cab.

1794
01:01:30,346 --> 01:01:33,456
Gosh. Isn't this the furthest we've ever walked?

1795
01:01:34,256 --> 01:01:35,485
It's not that bad.

1796
01:01:35,486 --> 01:01:37,226
You could've gone along with me.

1797
01:01:37,656 --> 01:01:41,025
I'm speaking out loud what Hyun Jin and Chun Hee think.

1798
01:01:41,026 --> 01:01:42,925
You don't get my intentions.

1799
01:01:42,926 --> 01:01:45,666
I was thinking, "Do they walk this far all the time?"

1800
01:01:45,736 --> 01:01:46,996
- It's a bit...
- Let's cross.

1801
01:01:47,296 --> 01:01:49,436
- It's a perfect day for walking.
- It's great.

1802
01:01:50,436 --> 01:01:52,206
- This is it.
- Where?

1803
01:01:52,436 --> 01:01:54,206
There should be fluffballs.

1804
01:01:54,336 --> 01:01:55,946
What fluffballs? This cafe?

1805
01:01:56,346 --> 01:01:58,306
- This should be...
- Fluffballs...

1806
01:01:59,616 --> 01:02:00,816
That must be it.

1807
01:02:00,976 --> 01:02:03,046
- Gosh. The puppies.
- There are many dogs.

1808
01:02:03,586 --> 01:02:05,015
- Gosh.
- Exactly. The fluffballs.

1809
01:02:05,016 --> 01:02:06,416
Hello. Gosh.

1810
01:02:06,916 --> 01:02:09,286
- Hello.
- Fluffballs. Gosh. What?

1811
01:02:09,386 --> 01:02:10,956
I think they're siblings.

1812
01:02:11,056 --> 01:02:12,256
Are they siblings? What?

1813
01:02:12,396 --> 01:02:13,726
- Is this a club?
- There are so many dogs.

1814
01:02:14,226 --> 01:02:16,595
- Gosh.
- Goodness. Hello.

1815
01:02:16,596 --> 01:02:17,766
- What's going on?
- Kwon Soon Ah?

1816
01:02:17,996 --> 01:02:19,136
- Kwon Soon Ah?
- Okay.

1817
01:02:20,766 --> 01:02:22,636
- Why are there so many dogs?
- This is...

1818
01:02:23,066 --> 01:02:24,105
Hey, guys.

1819
01:02:24,106 --> 01:02:25,476
- It's okay.
- You're happy to see them.

1820
01:02:25,606 --> 01:02:27,775
- Goodness.
- You're so happy.

1821
01:02:27,776 --> 01:02:29,175
- This is...
- Gosh.

1822
01:02:29,176 --> 01:02:31,075
- Yes.
- How to be cute?

1823
01:02:31,076 --> 01:02:32,845
- Gosh.
- Good job.

1824
01:02:32,846 --> 01:02:35,216
- Bitnam. They're wearing name tags.
- Yes.

1825
01:02:35,886 --> 01:02:36,945
(Yu Jin, Eun Hee, Hye Jin, )

1826
01:02:36,946 --> 01:02:37,986
(Hyeon Jeong, Soon Ah, Hye Mi)

1827
01:02:38,016 --> 01:02:39,215
(Teunteun, Hoya, Hanbit, Gyeoul, Bitnam, Chamee)

1828
01:02:39,216 --> 01:02:40,455
- Good.
- Good boy.

1829
01:02:40,456 --> 01:02:42,015
- Come here, Teunteun.
- Come here.

1830
01:02:42,016 --> 01:02:43,456
Come, Gyeoul.

1831
01:02:43,686 --> 01:02:45,395
- Good job.
- Hoya, here.

1832
01:02:45,396 --> 01:02:46,625
Come and sit.

1833
01:02:46,626 --> 01:02:47,925
Good girl.

1834
01:02:47,926 --> 01:02:49,325
- Park.
- Sit.

1835
01:02:49,326 --> 01:02:50,726
- Park.
- Good job.

1836
01:02:51,366 --> 01:02:53,295
- Gosh. They've calmed down.
- Yes.

1837
01:02:53,296 --> 01:02:54,596
Well done.

1838
01:02:54,896 --> 01:02:56,766
Gosh. Look at those eyes.

1839
01:02:57,036 --> 01:02:59,076
- Good.
- They're so close to one another.

1840
01:02:59,876 --> 01:03:00,935
It's unbelievable.

1841
01:03:00,936 --> 01:03:03,146
(Six dogs are gathered together.)

1842
01:03:03,906 --> 01:03:07,075
There are a lot of people here.

1843
01:03:07,076 --> 01:03:08,446
Will you introduce yourselves to us?

1844
01:03:09,020 --> 01:03:10,820
Do you know about puppy raising?

1845
01:03:10,857 --> 01:03:12,587
Will you explain it to us?

1846
01:03:12,886 --> 01:03:14,885
Okay. To become a guide dog...

1847
01:03:14,886 --> 01:03:16,455
for someone who is visually impaired,

1848
01:03:16,456 --> 01:03:19,055
- from a very young age...
- They need to get trained.

1849
01:03:19,056 --> 01:03:23,266
Yes. In the homes of volunteers like us,

1850
01:03:23,326 --> 01:03:26,295
they get socialization training for a year...

1851
01:03:26,296 --> 01:03:28,295
- I see.
- by staying with us.

1852
01:03:28,296 --> 01:03:29,536
(Helping 7-8-week-old guide dog candidates socialize for 1 year)

1853
01:03:29,566 --> 01:03:31,535
- I see. You look after one...
- Yes.

1854
01:03:31,536 --> 01:03:33,675
- for a year for this puppy raising.
- Yes.

1855
01:03:33,676 --> 01:03:35,005
That's right.

1856
01:03:35,006 --> 01:03:37,306
- And you take them back.
- Yes.

1857
01:03:37,576 --> 01:03:39,675
- Jung Jae Hyung is a puppy raiser.
- You're right.

1858
01:03:39,676 --> 01:03:40,945
- Am I right?
- Yes.

1859
01:03:40,946 --> 01:03:42,345
- For Haedeum.
- Yes.

1860
01:03:42,346 --> 01:03:45,045
I see. Are they all working as guide dogs right now?

1861
01:03:45,046 --> 01:03:46,415
- No.
- No.

1862
01:03:46,416 --> 01:03:49,286
- They were done, so they came back.
- After a year.

1863
01:03:49,356 --> 01:03:50,525
(Are they back?)

1864
01:03:50,526 --> 01:03:52,595
Simply put, they went, "We don't want to do it."

1865
01:03:52,596 --> 01:03:54,025
- "I..."
- "It's not my forte."

1866
01:03:54,026 --> 01:03:55,595
- "This isn't for me."
- Exactly.

1867
01:03:55,596 --> 01:03:57,365
- "I want to go home now."
- They took the test, but...

1868
01:03:57,366 --> 01:03:58,366
Exactly.

1869
01:03:58,367 --> 01:04:00,435
- they thought it didn't suit them.
- No.

1870
01:04:00,436 --> 01:04:02,635
So they are the ones who came back.

1871
01:04:02,636 --> 01:04:04,465
- That's right.
- I get it now.

1872
01:04:04,466 --> 01:04:06,206
- I understand.
- Later...

1873
01:04:06,650 --> 01:04:10,160
Their puppy raisers have priority to adopt them.

1874
01:04:10,206 --> 01:04:13,245
We meet the criteria to adopt them.

1875
01:04:13,246 --> 01:04:15,275
Just like that, this became a meetup...

1876
01:04:15,276 --> 01:04:17,616
where we gather in this part of town.

1877
01:04:17,846 --> 01:04:21,185
Did you get to know one another while walking with the dogs?

1878
01:04:21,186 --> 01:04:22,385
- That's right.
- I see.

1879
01:04:22,386 --> 01:04:23,785
- Someone would say, - Really?

1880
01:04:23,786 --> 01:04:26,155
- "There are other puppy raisers."
- I see.

1881
01:04:26,156 --> 01:04:27,796
Then we would go and meet them.

1882
01:04:28,256 --> 01:04:30,165
We develop a strong sense...

1883
01:04:30,166 --> 01:04:31,895
- of camaraderie.
- Right.

1884
01:04:31,896 --> 01:04:32,965
- I bet you would.
- Yes.

1885
01:04:32,966 --> 01:04:35,396
- Now I understand.
- Yes.

1886
01:04:35,536 --> 01:04:36,965
They look close to one another.

1887
01:04:36,966 --> 01:04:38,065
- Yes.
- They're so close.

1888
01:04:38,066 --> 01:04:40,276
- It's because they meet a lot.
- That's true.

1889
01:04:40,606 --> 01:04:41,976
(Cuddled up together)

1890
01:04:42,036 --> 01:04:43,845
- It's true.
- They're not siblings, are they?

1891
01:04:43,846 --> 01:04:44,905
Are they all separate?

1892
01:04:44,906 --> 01:04:46,545
Actually, Teunteun...

1893
01:04:46,546 --> 01:04:47,946
- and Hanbit at the end...
- And Hanbit.

1894
01:04:48,246 --> 01:04:49,685
- They're...
- They're a mother and a son.

1895
01:04:49,686 --> 01:04:51,085
- Are they a mother and a son?
- I see.

1896
01:04:51,086 --> 01:04:52,115
Who's the mother?

1897
01:04:52,116 --> 01:04:53,885
- Hanbit.
- Hanbit is his mommy.

1898
01:04:53,886 --> 01:04:55,655
- Are they a mother and a son?
- Yes.

1899
01:04:55,656 --> 01:04:56,686
I see.

1900
01:04:56,986 --> 01:04:59,196
Hanbit knows that we're talking about her.

1901
01:04:59,626 --> 01:05:01,796
- Hanbit, we're talking about you.
- Yes.

1902
01:05:02,466 --> 01:05:03,866
She knows.

1903
01:05:04,296 --> 01:05:07,166
What do you do when you meet up?

1904
01:05:07,336 --> 01:05:09,235
The first thing we do...

1905
01:05:09,236 --> 01:05:11,965
is anything we can do with our dogs.

1906
01:05:11,966 --> 01:05:12,975
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1907
01:05:12,976 --> 01:05:14,676
There's Dog Patrol.

1908
01:05:14,976 --> 01:05:18,045
They protect the community.

1909
01:05:18,046 --> 01:05:20,276
- And?
- When there's a local festival,

1910
01:05:20,416 --> 01:05:23,016
- Yes.
- we go and support it.

1911
01:05:23,146 --> 01:05:24,816
- What are these local festivals?
- Well...

1912
01:05:25,386 --> 01:05:27,716
For example, we go to a craft beer festival.

1913
01:05:27,916 --> 01:05:29,555
Yes. We join a craft beer festival.

1914
01:05:29,556 --> 01:05:31,555
There's a dog festival in Nowon-gu.

1915
01:05:31,556 --> 01:05:33,525
We participate in it too.

1916
01:05:33,526 --> 01:05:35,126
Is keeping order their job?

1917
01:05:35,866 --> 01:05:38,295
- Actually, being cute is their job.
- I see.

1918
01:05:38,296 --> 01:05:40,335
They participate in various activities...

1919
01:05:40,336 --> 01:05:41,936
- for these events.
- Yes.

1920
01:05:42,136 --> 01:05:43,765
When we need certifications...

1921
01:05:43,766 --> 01:05:46,776
For example, we all got the pet-sitter certifications.

1922
01:05:46,836 --> 01:05:49,905
We're also doing animal-assisted activities together.

1923
01:05:49,906 --> 01:05:52,005
- They do a lot of things.
- Yes.

1924
01:05:52,006 --> 01:05:54,175
Is that why they're wearing school uniforms?

1925
01:05:54,176 --> 01:05:56,345
- Is that why?
- Yes, this is spring-fall uniform.

1926
01:05:56,346 --> 01:05:57,346
- Really?
- It's so cute.

1927
01:05:57,347 --> 01:05:58,885
- We had it custom-made.
- I see.

1928
01:05:58,886 --> 01:06:00,685
Yes. We have a summer uniform too.

1929
01:06:00,686 --> 01:06:03,126
I don't know if I can mention it, but it looks like Burberry's.

1930
01:06:03,486 --> 01:06:04,785
Yes. We did that on purpose.

1931
01:06:04,786 --> 01:06:05,995
- Yes.
- Yes. That's true.

1932
01:06:05,996 --> 01:06:07,625
- That was the concept.
- That was.

1933
01:06:07,626 --> 01:06:08,966
Gosh. It's so cute.

1934
01:06:09,826 --> 01:06:11,366
Do you like it, Yeon Seok?

1935
01:06:11,726 --> 01:06:13,635
- What? Which one?
- We heard you have a dog.

1936
01:06:13,636 --> 01:06:14,636
- Rita?
- We heard about your Rita.

1937
01:06:14,637 --> 01:06:16,035
- Yes, I have Rita.
- Isn't she pretty?

1938
01:06:16,036 --> 01:06:17,935
- I adopted her.
- Wait. Really?

1939
01:06:17,936 --> 01:06:19,775
- We knew it.
- Is there something for me?

1940
01:06:19,776 --> 01:06:21,676
- We knew it.
- We knew it.

1941
01:06:22,006 --> 01:06:24,376
- Gosh. What?
- Goodness.

1942
01:06:24,976 --> 01:06:27,115
- Gosh. Yeon Seok got a gift.
- A school uniform?

1943
01:06:27,116 --> 01:06:28,516
She has a school uniform now.

1944
01:06:28,816 --> 01:06:30,546
I'm happy to get Rita's clothes.

1945
01:06:31,546 --> 01:06:33,286
- It even comes with a name tag.
- Yes.

1946
01:06:33,516 --> 01:06:35,356
- It's really cute.
- It's pretty.

1947
01:06:35,586 --> 01:06:37,055
She's like, "Who's Rita?"

1948
01:06:37,056 --> 01:06:38,785
Why are you showing interest?

1949
01:06:38,786 --> 01:06:40,555
- They're saying it's their uniform.
- Gosh.

1950
01:06:40,556 --> 01:06:41,626
- Goodness.
- It's the sound of a bag.

1951
01:06:41,756 --> 01:06:43,325
They think it's their treat because of the rustling sound.

1952
01:06:43,326 --> 01:06:45,526
They think it's their treat.

1953
01:06:45,796 --> 01:06:47,696
- No, it's not.
- Because of the rustling bag.

1954
01:06:47,896 --> 01:06:50,005
- Seo Hanbit, sit.
- Because of the rustling bag.

1955
01:06:50,006 --> 01:06:51,805
- Yes.
- Hanbit, come here.

1956
01:06:51,806 --> 01:06:52,835
(She won't budge.)

1957
01:06:52,836 --> 01:06:55,205
The mother and the son...

1958
01:06:55,206 --> 01:06:56,446
are into eating...

1959
01:06:56,946 --> 01:06:58,406
just like humans are.

1960
01:06:58,906 --> 01:07:01,015
- They were simultaneous.
- They're obsessed with food.

1961
01:07:01,016 --> 01:07:02,145
Really?

1962
01:07:02,146 --> 01:07:04,716
Thank you. I'll give it to Rita.

1963
01:07:05,246 --> 01:07:07,355
(Rita pulls off the fall uniform.)

1964
01:07:07,356 --> 01:07:09,285
They are all sitting right now.

1965
01:07:09,286 --> 01:07:10,785
- I can't believe it.
- It looks very peaceful.

1966
01:07:10,786 --> 01:07:12,255
- But it isn't easy.
- It isn't easy.

1967
01:07:12,256 --> 01:07:15,055
Right. Actually, this isn't a sight you see often.

1968
01:07:15,056 --> 01:07:17,165
Seriously. It really isn't easy...

1969
01:07:17,166 --> 01:07:19,335
for all of them to keep calm and behave.

1970
01:07:19,336 --> 01:07:20,635
- They're all calm, right?
- Yes.

